##############################################
### IMPORT/EXPORT ENDPOINTS
##############################################

### Export All Products to JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/export?uploadToBlob=true
Accept: application/json

###

### Export All Products (No Blob Upload)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/export?uploadToBlob=false
Accept: application/json

###

### Import Products from JSON File
### Note: Use your API testing tool (Postman, Insomnia, etc.) for file upload
### Or use curl:
### curl -X POST "{{baseUrl}}/api/products/import?uploadToBlob=true" \
###   -H "Content-Type: multipart/form-data" \
###   -F "file=@SampleData/products.json"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/import?uploadToBlob=true
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="products.json"
Content-Type: application/json

< ./SampleData/products.json
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

###

### List Import Files in Blob Storage
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/import/files
Accept: application/json

###

### Import Products from Blob Storage File
### Replace 'import_20240115_120000.json' with an actual file name from the list above
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/import/blob/import_20240115_120000.json
Content-Type: application/json

###
